#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""crotate — standalone multi-account /rotate for Claude Code + Codex.

The rotate feature of neomax-orchestrator, extracted to run WITHOUT neomax /
the orchestrator: store several Claude Max + Codex accounts on one machine and
swap a live session's account in place (no /login, no OAuth click) when it
nears its 5-hour or weekly usage limit — manually via /rotate, hands-off via
an armed per-turn Stop hook, and (for already-rate-limited sessions that can
never end a turn) via a model-free launchd tick.

Accounts (same isolation scheme as cmax):
  claude: acct 1 = ~/.claude (CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR unset), acct N = ~/.claude-acctN
          (CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR namespaces the macOS Keychain item per profile)
  codex:  acct 1 = ~/.codex,  acct N = ~/.codex-acctN  (CODEX_HOME; file auth)

State lives in ~/.crotate (override: CROTATE_HOME) — independent of ~/.neomax.
Test hooks: CROTATE_PROFILES / CROTATE_CODEX_PROFILES (colon-separated profile
dirs), CROTATE_NO_KEYCHAIN=1 (skip `security`, file-store only).

Commands:
  crotate status [--json]                    account board, both engines
  crotate session-rotate [<acct>...] [--engine claude|codex] [--threshold N]
                         [--weekly-threshold N] [--arm] [--dry-run]
                                             the /rotate engine (pure python,
                                             works even when rate-limited)
  crotate disarm [--engine E] [--profile P]  clear an armed auto-rotation
  crotate tick [--active]                    one model-free rotation sweep
                                             (the launchd agent runs this)
  crotate usage-hook                         Claude Stop-hook entrypoint
  crotate login N [--engine claude|codex]    authenticate account N
  crotate run [--engine E] N [args...]       plain interactive session on account N
                                             (the claudeN/codexN helpers call this)
  crotate rotate-auth <dest> --from <src> [--engine E] [--swap]
  crotate rotate-auth --restore <dest> [--engine E]
  crotate log                                recent rotations
  crotate pause N | unpause N [--engine E]   exclude/include an account
  crotate portal [--port 8787] [--no-open]   read-only localhost dashboard (opens browser)
"""

